<section class="ref-group"><h2>Battles <span class="n">36</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-catraeth"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-catraeth.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Catraeth</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 600</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Catraeth was fought around 600 between a war band of the British kingdom of Gododdin and the Angles of Deira and Bernicia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-degsastan"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Degsastan</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 603</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Degsastan was fought in 603 between Æthelfrith of Bernicia and Áedán mac Gabráin, king of Dál Riata, who led a large army including Irish allies.…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dhi-qar"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Dhi Qar</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 609</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Dhi Qar was fought in southern Iraq in the early 7th century, probably between 604 and 611, between Arab tribes led by the Banu Shayban and a Sasanian…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-salsu"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Salsu</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 612</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Salsu was fought in 612 when Goguryeo forces under Eulji Mundeok destroyed a large Sui army as it retreated across the Salsu river, usually identified…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chester"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Chester</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 615</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Chester was fought around 615 near Chester, where Æthelfrith of Northumbria defeated the Britons of Powys and their allies.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pullalur"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Pullalur</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 618–619</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Pullalur was fought around 618–619 near Kanchipuram between the Pallava king Mahendravarman I and the Chalukya king Pulakeshin II, who had invaded Pallava…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-qianshuiyuan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-qianshuiyuan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Qianshuiyuan</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 618</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Qianshuiyuan was fought in 618 in the north of modern Shaanxi between the new Tang dynasty and the Qin state of Xue Ju and his son Xue Rengao.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hulao"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-hulao.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Hulao</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 621</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Hulao was fought in 621 at the Hulao Pass, a fortified gap west of modern Zhengzhou in Henan, during the wars that followed the fall of the Sui dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-uhud"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-uhud.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Uhud</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 625</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Uhud was fought in March 625 at Mount Uhud, north of Medina, between the Muslims under Muhammad and the Quraysh of Mecca led by Abu Sufyan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nineveh-627"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Nineveh (627)</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 627 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Nineveh was fought in 627 CE near the ruins of ancient Nineveh in northern Mesopotamia, where the Byzantine emperor Heraclius defeated a Sasanian army.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-wogastisburg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-wogastisburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Wogastisburg</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 631 or 632</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Wogastisburg was fought in 631 or 632 between the Slavs led by Samo and the army of the Frankish king Dagobert I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hatfield-chase"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-hatfield-chase.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Hatfield Chase</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 633</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Hatfield Chase was fought in 633 near Doncaster in Yorkshire, where Cadwallon ap Cadfan of Gwynedd and Penda of Mercia defeated and killed Edwin, the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-heavenfield"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-heavenfield.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Heavenfield</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 634</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Heavenfield was fought in 634 near Hexham in Northumberland, where Oswald of Bernicia defeated and killed Cadwallon ap Cadfan of Gwynedd, who had ravaged…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-al-qadisiyyah"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-al-qadisiyyah.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of al-Qadisiyyah</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 636 or 637 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of al-Qadisiyyah was fought in 636 or