ates in Syria between the caliph Ali and Mu'awiya, the governor of Syria, during the First Fitna.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hwangsanbeol"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-hwangsanbeol.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Hwangsanbeol</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 660</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Hwangsanbeol was fought in 660 near present-day Nonsan in South Korea between a large Silla army under Kim Yu-sin and a small Baekje force led by General…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-baekgang"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-baekgang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Baekgang</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 663</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Baekgang was fought in 663 near the mouth of the Geum river in south-western Korea between Tang Chinese and Silla forces and the fleet of Yamato Japan…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dafei-river"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-dafei-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Dafei River</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 670</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Dafei River was fought in 670 near Lake Kokonor in present-day Qinghai, China.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-maeso-fortress"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Maeso Fortress</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 675</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Maeso Fortress was fought in 675 at Maesoseong, a fortress north of present-day Seoul, between Silla and a Tang Chinese army.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gibeolpo"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Gibeolpo</span><span c