aign against the Eastern Turks was a military expedition launched by Emperor Taizong that defeated the Eastern Turkic Khaganate in 630 CE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ridda-wars"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ridda-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ridda Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War · 632–633 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ridda Wars, or Wars of Apostasy, were a series of campaigns fought in 632–633 CE by the first caliph, Abu Bakr, against Arabian tribes that broke away after the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/muslim-conquest-of-persia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/muslim-conquest-of-persia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Muslim conquest of Persia</span><span class="enc-type">War · 633–654</span><span class="enc-snip">The Muslim conquest of Persia was the conquest of the Sasanian Empire by the Rashidun Caliphate between 633 and the early 650s.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/muslim-conquest-of-the-levant-and-egypt"><span class="enc-name">Muslim conquest of the Levant and Egypt</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 637–642 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Muslim conquest of the Levant and Egypt refers to the Arab campaigns that took Syria, Palestine and Egypt from Byzantine control in the seventh century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/arab-conquest-of-the-fezzan"><span class="enc-name">Arab conquest of the Fezzan</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 643–670 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Arab conquest of the Fezzan was the series of Muslim Arab campaigns into the Fezzan region of south-western Libya between 643 and 670 CE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/muslim-conquest-of-the-maghreb"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs